{"name":"Eternal Flame","hex":"#a13f49","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eternal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Lasting forever; unending.","Existing outside time; as opposed to sempiternal, existing within time but everlastingly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who lives forever; an immortal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eternal"},{"term":"flame","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The visible part of fire; a stream of burning vapour or gas, emitting light and heat.","A romantic partner or lover in a usually short-lived but passionate affair."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a brilliant reddish orange-gold colour, like that of a flame."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flame"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eternal Flame (Azerbaijan)","blocks":[{"text":"Eternal Flame is a monument that was established for the Azerbaijanis who died during Black January. The monument is situated in Martyrs’ Line, Baku. Every year Azerbaijanis commemorate Black January in that place."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Ilham_Aliyev_paid_tribute_to_martyrs_of_January_20%2C_2019_09_%28crop%29.jpg/330px-Ilham_Aliyev_paid_tribute_to_martyrs_of_January_20%2C_2019_09_%28crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eternal_Flame_(Azerbaijan)"},{"title":"Eternal Flame (Bangladesh)","blocks":[{"text":"The Eternal Flame also known as Shikha Chironton is a historical landmark of Bangladesh. The flame was created to keep alive the memory of the martyrs who lost their lives in the Liberation War of Bangladesh and the defeat of the Pakistani Forces. It was jointly opened on March 26, 1997, on the occasion of Bangladesh independence day by then Prime minister of Bangladesh Sheikh Hasina, the President of South Africa Nelson Mandela, the President of Palestine Yasir Arafat and the President of Turkiye Süleyman Demirel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/The_Universal_Flame.jpg/330px-The_Universal_Flame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eternal_Flame_(Bangladesh)"},{"title":"Eternal Flame (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Eternal Flame\" is a song by American pop rock group the Bangles for their third studio album, Everything (1988). Released on January 23, 1989, by CBS, the power ballad was written by group member Susanna Hoffs with the established hit songwriting team of Billy Steinberg and Tom Kelly. Davitt Sigerson produced it."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/Eternal_Flame_by_The_Bangles_US_commercial_cassette.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eternal_Flame_(song)"},{"title":"Eternal flame","blocks":[{"text":"An eternal flame is a flame, lamp or torch that burns for an indefinite time. Most eternal flames are ignited and tended intentionally. However, some are natural phenomena caused by natural gas leaks, peat fires and coal seam fires, all of which can be initially ignited by lightning, piezoelectricity or human activity, some of which have burned for hundreds or thousands of years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Nizhny_Novgorod_Eternal_Flame_01.JPG/330px-Nizhny_Novgorod_Eternal_Flame_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eternal_flame"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Dmitry_Medvedev_in_Azerbaijan_3_July_2008-8.jpg/250px-Dmitry_Medvedev_in_Azerbaijan_3_July_2008-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c7/Dmitry_Medvedev_in_Azerbaijan_3_July_2008-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Dmitry_Medvedev_in_Azerbaijan_3_July_2008-8.jpg/250px-Dmitry_Medvedev_in_Azerbaijan_3_July_2008-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADmitry_Medvedev_in_Azerbaijan_3_July_2008-8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/%E0%A6%B6%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%96%E0%A6%BE_%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A7%A8.jpg/500px-%E0%A6%B6%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%96%E0%A6%BE_%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A7%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/%E0%A6%B6%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%96%E0%A6%BE_%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A7%A8.jpg/1280px-%E0%A6%B6%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%96%E0%A6%BE_%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A7%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/%E0%A6%B6%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%96%E0%A6%BE_%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A7%A8.jpg/500px-%E0%A6%B6%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%96%E0%A6%BE_%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A7%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eternal Flame","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E0%A6%B6%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%96%E0%A6%BE_%E0%A6%9A%E0%A6%BF%E0%A6%B0%E0%A6%A8%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%A4%E0%A6%A8_%E0%A7%A8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Shikha_Chironton%2C_Suhrawardy_Udyan%2C_Dhaka.jpg/500px-Shikha_Chironton%2C_Suhrawardy_Udyan%2C_Dhaka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Shikha_Chironto